---
layout: default
---
{% comment %}
  A category's page (/blog/category/<name>/, made by jekyll-archives): its posts as the same rows as the blog. The
  name shown is the chip's label from _data/blog.yml.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign label = page.title | replace: '-', ' ' | capitalize %}
{% for chip in site.data.blog.chips %}
  {% if chip.category == page.title %}{% assign label = chip.label %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
<div class="post">
  <header class="post-header">
    <h1 class="post-title">{{ label }}</h1>
    <p class="post-description">
      {{ page.posts.size }} {% if page.posts.size == 1 %}post{% else %}posts{% endif %} ·
      <a href="{{ '/' | relative_url }}">all posts</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  {% include blog_index.liquid posts=page.posts mode="category" %}
</div>
